# Build context for the root Dockerfile. Only three trees are actually needed:
# pyproject.toml + README.md + engine/ (the pip install), service/, and frontend/
# (the node build stage). Everything else is noise that slows the context upload
# and, worse, can silently end up in the published image.

# --- version control, editors, CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/

# --- Python build and cache artefacts ---
# NOTE: .dockerignore patterns are root-relative, NOT recursive like .gitignore.
# A bare `node_modules/` only excludes the one at the top of the context; the
# `**/` forms below are what actually keep nested trees out.
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Node ---
# frontend/ itself is the build stage's input; only its generated trees are
# excluded. `**/` matters here: a stray nested project (an untracked scratch
# checkout under frontend/, say) otherwise pushes hundreds of MB of
# node_modules through the build context and into the frontend stage.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
frontend/dist/

# --- tests: not packaged (packages.find looks under engine/) and not run in the image ---
engine/tests/
service/tests/
googleapps/tests/

# --- vendored reference code: read-only, imported by nothing (see CLAUDE.md) ---
vendor/

# --- retired pre-rewrite code: not linted, not packaged, not imported ---
frontend-archive/
backend/
mcp/
pcb/
packing/
footprint/
lib_pickle_dir/
lcsc.py
test_skidl.py
test_skidl_sklib.py

# --- docs, design sources, dev scripts: none of it is served or imported ---
docs/
design/
scripts/
*.md
!README.md
TODO.txt
LICENSE

# --- generated boards and EDA scratch output ---
*.kicad_pcb
*.kicad_sch
*.kicad_pro
*.net
*.erc
*.log
*.pkl

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances, in a published image ---
.env
.env.*

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
